    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 2026-10-15; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Alert, direct, and well-appearing; weight stable from the summer</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Pupils equal and reactive; no injection or discharge in the left eye after recent injections; acuity is followed by her retina specialist (77 ETDRS letters in the right eye and 70 in the left in July)</td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Canals clear; whispered-voice test passed on both sides</td></tr><tr><td>Neck</td><td>No thyroid enlargement or nodes; no carotid bruits</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Regular rhythm; no murmur; pedal pulses present; no edema</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Clear to auscultation bilaterally</td></tr><tr><td>Abdomen</td><td>Soft and non-tender; no masses</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Left ankle stable with full range of motion and no tenderness; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds with a steady gait; rises from a chair without using her arms; holds a tandem stance for 10 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Oriented; Mini-Cog 5 of 5 (recall 3 of 3; clock drawn with a bold marker under task lighting, normal)</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Euthymic and engaged; judgment and insight intact</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>Sun-weathered skin on the face and hands; no suspicious lesions</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

