<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed, personalized prevention plan updated, and a written copy given in large print. Depression, alcohol, and cognitive screens are negative. Fall risk is increased because of a fall with injury this year and reduced contrast vision. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Neovascular age-related macular degeneration, left eye (H35.3221)</content>. Stable on treat-and-extend aflibercept by her report, with no new distortion on daily Amsler checks. [S]<list><item>Continue injections and monitoring with her retina specialist.</item><item>Continue daily Amsler grid checks and call the same day for any change.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Intermediate dry age-related macular degeneration, right eye (H35.3112)</content>. No new symptoms; this eye carries most of her reading and driving vision. [S]<list><item>Continue the AREDS2 supplement.</item><item>Dilated examination of the right eye continues at each retina visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk, increased</content>. One fall with injury in the past year, caused by an unseen edge in low-contrast light rather than weakness or dizziness. Timed Up and Go is 11 seconds and balance is good, but low vision and living alone raise both the chance and the consequences of a fall. [S]<list><item>Refer to physical therapy for a progressive balance and strength exercise program.</item><item>Home safety: brighter, glare-free lighting in the hallway and at the studio step, high-contrast tape on the step edge, remove the two loose rugs, grab bars by the toilet and in the shower, and night lights on the route to the bathroom.</item><item>Personal emergency alert pendant or a phone carried at all times, including on walks.</item><item>Ask the low-vision rehabilitation team for an updated home visit as her vision changes.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Driving with reduced central vision</content>. She drives short local routes by day only, after the driving assessment done during low-vision rehabilitation. Her right eye carries her driving vision. [S]<list><item>Continue daytime local driving only; no driving at night, at dawn or dusk, or in rain.</item><item>Stop driving and call if the right eye develops new distortion or blur, and reassess driving whenever her retina specialist reports a drop in acuity.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, current season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Second dose given today, seven months after the first; the series is complete and does not need to restart</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>No pneumococcal vaccine on record; one dose of a conjugate vaccine is recommended at 50 or older. Planned at a nurse visit next month</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>No RSV vaccine on record; a single dose is recommended at 75 or older. Planned at the same nurse visit</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Due</td><td>No tetanus booster on record; Td or Tdap at the nurse visit</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, current season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at her age; she will get it at her pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No prior scan on record; recommended for women 65 and older, and her fall with injury and low body weight raise the stakes of a fracture</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1, negative</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5, with the clock drawn under task lighting</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Referred</td><td>Fall with injury this year; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; physical therapy referral for balance and strength exercise and written home-safety changes</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Seen regularly by her retina specialist, with dilated examination of both eyes</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Whispered-voice test passed on both sides</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and diabetes screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No lipid panel or glucose on record; ordered with the next blood draw. Any statin decision at her age would be shared</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Screening is selective from 76 to 85; after discussion she prefers not to continue</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Evidence is insufficient after 75; after discussion she prefers not to have further mammograms</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 65 with adequate prior screening</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Physical therapy referral and DXA scan ordered; lipid panel and glucose with the next blood draw. Nurse visit next month for pneumococcal, RSV, and tetanus vaccines. Retina care continues on its own schedule. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
